-----|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|\nDESCENDING - 12 GROUPS / 48 NOTES\nPos|15-14-13-12-|14-13-12-11-|13-12-11-10-|12-11-10-9--|11-10-9--8--|10-9--8--7--|9--8--7--6--|8--7--6--5--|7--6--5--4--|6--5--4--3--|5--4--3--2--|4--3--2--1--|\nFng|1--4--2--1--|4--2--1--4--|2--1--4--2--|1--4--2--1--|4--2--1--3--|2--1--3--1--|1--3--1--4--|3--1--4--3--|1--4--3--1--|4--3--1--4--|3--1--4--3--|1--4--3--1--|\ne  |5-----------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|\nB  |---8--6--5--|8--6--5-----|6--5--------|5-----------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|\nG  |------------|---------7--|------7--5--|---7--5--4--|7--5--4-----|5--4--------|4-----------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|\nD  |------------|------------|------------|------------|---------7--|------7--5--|---7--5-----|7--5--------|5-----------|------------|------------|------------|\nA  |------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|---------8--|------8--7--|---8--7--5--|8--7--5-----|7--5--------|5-----------|\nE  |------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|---------8--|------8--7--|---8--7--5--|\nPAGE-TO-PAGE TRANSITION\nModule 3 ends on the low root. Turn the page without moving the frame. Re-articulate the same low root as the first note of module 4 and continue the alternate-picking cycle.\nRung 01: A natural minor. Modules 1-3 contain 204 notes; the hand remains in frame 4-8.\nPage 3 of 31\n","text_sha256":"ec4bb4e8292011c4a2fdc70b666b9d38d1a72ddcfe082eccff39410c070460b9"},"L29-PDF-PULSE-P2":{"format":"pdf","page":2,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/PDF version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_29_Natural_Minor_Synthesis_Circuit_Two_Octave_Six_String_Neck_Ladder.pdf","sha256":"2310fc942262081445d80d164ae6feab6335a879db283863db27f69bb75ef445","text":"Level 29 - Circuit Map, Pulse Plan, and Chromatic Route\nAscending route: finish one 322-note circuit, then move the complete frame +1 fret\nDescending route: use the same rung pages in reverse order and move -1 fret\nRung\nKey\nLow-E root\nFrame\nCell\nShift after\n01\nA natural minor\nfret 5\n4-8\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n02\nBb natural minor\nfret 6\n5-9\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n03\nB natural minor\nfret 7\n6-10\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n04\nC natural minor\nfret 8\n7-11\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n05\nC# natural minor\nfret 9\n8-12\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n06\nD natural minor\nfret 10\n9-13\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n07\nEb natural minor\nfret 11\n10-14\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n08\nE natural minor\nfret 12\n11-15\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n09\nF natural minor\nfret 13\n12-16\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n10\nF# natural minor\nfret 14\n13-17\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n11\nG natural minor\nfret 15\n14-18\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n12\nG# natural minor\nfret 16\n15-19\n322 notes\nmodule 5\n13\nA natural minor - octave\nfret 17\n16-20\n322 notes\nmodule 5\nPulse plan\nA\n30 notes\n15 beats\n2 per beat\nB\n78 notes\n26 beats\n3 per beat\nC\n96 notes\n24 beats\n4 per beat\nD\n52 notes\n26 beats\n2 per beat\nE\n66 notes\n22 beats\n3 per beat\nTOTAL\n113 beats\nRoute count\n25 cells\n13 up + 12 down\n8,050 notes\nfull A-to-A-to-A route\nCircuit anatomy\nMODULE ORDER\nA linear -> B three-note -> C four-note -> D thirds -> E triads\nBOUNDARY ROOT\nEvery module ends on the low root and the next module re-articulates that same root.\nPICKING\nAll five module counts are even. Every module and every new key begins on the original start stroke.\nSHIFT\nRelease pressure and move one fret only after the final 5-b3-1 triad of module E.\nLEARNING MODE\nUse one note per click first; then adopt the native subdivisions shown in the pulse plan.\nStandard tuning. Same two-octave sixth-string-root natural-minor frame used throughout Levels 22, 24, 26, 27, and 28.\nPage 2 of 31\n","text_sha256":"4e589a30a238dc3e6dbadb2764684d3f981ef575d1e46f0ee0a6b423d43fb3ae"},"L29-TXT-RULES-1-46":{"first_line":1,"format":"txt","last_line":46,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_29_Natural_Minor_Synthesis_Circuit_Two_Octave_Six_String_Neck_Ladder.txt","sha256":"543d98fa9279f39d8975d6b00cd43e5f5aebbb94c5e59fe7771f63af8d8244e5","text":"SCALE EXERCISES - SECTION III, LEVEL 29\nNATURAL MINOR SYNTHESIS CIRCUIT - TWO-OCTAVE SIX-STRING NECK LADDER\n================================================================================================================================================================\n\nPURPOSE\nLevel 29 combines the established two-octave natural-minor movements from Levels 22, 24, 26, 27, and 28 into\none uninterrupted circuit. Complete all five modules in the same key before shifting the entire hand-and-thumb\nframe one fret. Re-articulate the low root at every module boundary while preserving the alternate-picking cycle.\n\nFIVE-MODULE CELL\nA. Linear scale:          30 notes - low root to high root, repeat high root, return to low root\nB. Three-note roll:       78 notes - 13 ascending triplets and 13 descending triplets\nC. Four-note roll:        96 notes - 12 ascending groups and 12 descending groups\nD. Diatonic thirds:       52 notes - 13 ascending pairs and 13 descending pairs\nE. Diatonic triads:       66 notes - 11 ascending triads and 11 descending triads\nTOTAL:                   322 notes per key\n\nMODULE ORDER\nLinear -> Three-note roll -> Four-note roll -> Diatonic thirds -> Diatonic triads -> shift one fret\n\nNATURAL-MINOR FORMULA\nOne octave: 1 2 b3 4 5 b6 b7 8\nTwo octaves: 1 2 b3 4 5 b6 b7 8 9 b10 11 12 b13 b14 15\nIntervals: whole - half - whole - whole - half - whole - whole, then repeat\n\nPICKING\nAll five module counts are even. With a downstroke start, every module and every new key begins on a downstroke;\nwith an upstroke start, each begins on an upstroke. Do not reset at group boundaries, string changes, octave turns,\nmodule boundaries, the G-string backreach, the B-string offset, or one-fret shifts.\n\nRHYTHM\nLearning mode: one note per metronome click through the complete circuit.\nNative-pulse mode:\n- Linear scale: 30 eighth notes = 15 beats\n- Three-note roll: 78 eighth-note triplets = 26 beats\n- Four-note roll: 96 sixteenth notes = 24 beats\n- Diatonic thirds: 52 eighth notes = 26 beats\n- Diatonic triads: 66 eighth-note triplets = 22 beats\nTOTAL: 113 quarter-note beats per 322-note circuit\n\nPRACTICE PROGRESSION\n1. Learn each module separately in A natural minor.\n2. Link adjacent module pairs: A-B, B-C, C-D, and D-E.\n3. Play the complete A-natural-minor circuit with a short pause at every module boundary.\n4. Remove the pauses while retaining a light accent on each new module root.\n5. Remove the accents and use two or three neighboring keys.","text_sha256":"39a0ac513f557180e05062813bed4921005cea8c98f60c26553c3eaa60069684"},"L29-TXT-RUNG01-80-95":{"first_line":80,"format":"txt","last_line":95,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_29_Natural_Minor_Synthesis_Circuit_Two_Octave_Six_String_Neck_Ladder.txt","sha256":"543d98fa9279f39d8975d6b00cd43e5f5aebbb94c5e59fe7771f63af8d8244e5","text":"================================================================================================================================================================\nRUNG 01 OF 13 - A NATURAL MINOR - ROOT ON LOW E FRET 5 - FRAME 4-8\nScale tones across two octaves: A B C D E F G A B C D E F G A\nDiatonic triads: Am | Bdim | C | Dm | Em | F | G\n322-note synthesis circuit: play modules 1-5 without stopping, then shift one fret.\n\nMODULE 1 - LINEAR SCALE - 30 NOTES\nDeg|1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--2--b3-4--5--b6-b7-1--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--b7-b6-5--4--b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--1--3--4--1--3--1--2--4--1--2--4--1--1--4--2--1--4--2--1--3--1--4--3--1--4--3--1--|\ne  |------------------------------------------5--5--------------------------------------------|\nB  |---------------------------------5--6--8--------8--6--5-----------------------------------|\nG  |------------------------4--5--7--------------------------7--5--4--------------------------|\nD  |------------------5--7--------------------------------------------7--5--------------------|\nA  |---------5--7--8--------------------------------------------------------8--7--5-----------|\nE  |5--7--8--------------------------------------------------------------------------8--7--5--|\nRe-articulate the low root immediately and continue into module 2 without resetting the pick cycle.","text_sha256":"2b14f160457013f5e5703063305f916b4c747ed674c1de51c97ed259dfd16776"}}}
